 "note": "One table, two implementations: service/of_rich_text.py (has_html, of_text, of_plain) and app/lib/ofRichText.ts (hasHtml, ofText, ofPlain). service/tests/test_of_rich_text.py and app/lib/ofRichText.test.ts both assert every row; add a row here and whichever side drifts goes red. Bytes differ by design in one place, kept out of this table: the relay keeps tags nested as given (the app writes OF's span > strong > em). Also out of the table: entities without their `;` (`&amp b`, `&copy2024`) and numeric C1 references (`&#150;`) in markup — the relay decodes them as browsers do, the app keeps them as written; OF's and our editor's markup always writes `;`. Out of the table too: numeric references a browser reads as U+FFFD (`&#0;`, `&#xD800;`, `&#1114112;`) — the relay decodes them to U+FFFD, the app keeps them as written. A text that fails closed on a handler-shaped word (`<b>hi</b> online=yes`, the A4 row) is escaped whole: its bare tags show as written, nothing is lost.",
